## Lifecycle phases

This vault is organised around three phases. Planning is a light setup phase anchored on the Scope of Work. The bulk of day-to-day knowledge work then happens inside Delivery (Meetings, Correspondence, Analysis, Working Files). Reporting holds outputs and close-out artefacts.

| Phase | Folder | Hub | Anchor artefacts |
|-------|--------|-----|------------------|
| **1. Planning** | `Planning/` | [[Planning]] | Scope of Work, Team RACI, Session Schedule, Open Questions, Assumptions Log |
| **2. Delivery** | `Delivery/` | [[Delivery]] | Analysis hubs, Meetings, Correspondence, Working Files |
| **3. Reporting** | `Reporting/` | [[Reporting]] | Draft Report, Findings Log, Final Report, Debrief, Lessons Learned |

Cross-phase content (People, Entities, Concepts, References, Deliverables, Attachments) lives at the vault root because it is read from every phase. Meetings, Correspondence and Analysis live under Delivery because that is where the bulk of work happens; they carry `phase:` frontmatter so the Dashboard can render per-phase cuts.

