## Correspondence processing rules

1. **Extract contact details** (phone, title) from signatures.
2. **Update People files** with any new contact information found.
3. **Standardise the role or title** to the signature where it is more specific than what is on file.
4. File the processed item under `Delivery/Correspondence/` with `phase:` frontmatter.

## Vault log

`log.md` at the vault root is an append-only runtime log. Every skill that
mutates the vault appends an entry after finishing its work.

## Boundary rules

- **This vault may hold confidential material.** Do not write to other vaults
  from inside it without explicit approval, and check what leaves it.
- Reusable patterns that generalise are extracted into an operations vault
  after the project closes. The project vault then stops growing and becomes a
  record.

## Editing files outside the editor

Obsidian caches open files in memory, so a bulk edit made on disk while it is
running can be overwritten when it next writes. Quit it first, make the edits,
then reopen.

